# Entirely fictional symptom examples for classification, not diagnosis or triage.
# These descriptions cannot establish an illness or rule out serious causes.
# One item per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
For two days I have had a blocked nose, a scratchy throat and a mild cough after my flatmate had similar symptoms.
My nose has been running since yesterday, my throat feels scratchy and I have started coughing a little.
Over the last three days I developed sneezing, a stuffy nose and a mild sore throat.
I have a mild cough and a blocked nose that started gradually after a few days of throat irritation.
Every time I walk past the flowering trees my eyes itch and water and I start sneezing.
My nose runs with clear fluid and my eyes itch on high-pollen days, then improve when I stay indoors.
During grass-pollen season I sneeze repeatedly and get watery, itchy eyes while sitting in the park.
Opening the windows on spring mornings brings on sneezing and an itchy nose and eyes.
After a long afternoon at my desk I feel a mild tight band around both sides of my head and tense shoulders.
On stressful workdays a dull pressure builds around my forehead alongside tight neck muscles.
After hours of looking down at paperwork, both sides of my head feel mildly squeezed and my shoulders are tense.
I get a mild pressing feeling across my forehead after a day of tense meetings, rather than a throbbing pain.
After a very large evening meal I feel unusually full and bloated and keep belching.
A rich takeaway left me with mild upper-abdominal discomfort, fullness and frequent burping after eating.
I ate a heavy lunch quickly and now feel bloated with a full stomach and repeated belching.
After an extra helping of a rich meal, the top of my stomach feels uncomfortable and overfull.
Reading in the back seat on winding roads makes me queasy, and I feel better after the car stops.
I felt nauseated while the ferry was rocking and the queasiness eased after we reached land.
Looking at my phone on the bus makes my stomach turn, but the feeling settles when I get off.
On a long boat trip I became queasy with the waves and improved once we returned to the harbour.
I feel a bit off today but cannot describe any specific symptoms.
My head aches and my nose runs, but I have not noticed when it happens or any other details.
I have an itchy patch on my arm, with no other information about how it started.
My stomach feels odd sometimes; I have not noticed whether it relates to meals, travel or anything else.
